=== a value of the wrong type or out of range names the setting and the value
--- SELECT 1 SETTINGS max_threads = 'abc'
Code: 27. Cannot parse input: expected 'eof' before: 'abc': while setting 'max_threads' to value 'abc'. (CANNOT_PARSE_INPUT_ASSERTION_FAILED)
--- SELECT 1 SETTINGS max_threads = -1
Code: 70. Field value -1 is out of range of unsigned long type: while setting 'max_threads' to value -1. (CANNOT_CONVERT_TYPE)
--- SELECT 1 SETTINGS max_block_size = 0
Code: 36. A setting's value has to be greater than 0: while setting 'max_block_size' to value 0. (BAD_ARGUMENTS)
--- SELECT 1 SETTINGS max_memory_usage = '10 elephants'
Code: 27. Cannot parse input: expected 'eof' before: ' elephants': while setting 'max_memory_usage' to value '10 elephants'. (CANNOT_PARSE_INPUT_ASSERTION_FAILED)
--- SET max_threads = 'abc'
Code: 27. Cannot parse input: expected 'eof' before: 'abc': while setting 'max_threads' to value 'abc'. (CANNOT_PARSE_INPUT_ASSERTION_FAILED)

=== an unknown setting keeps the message it had, with no context appended
code: UNKNOWN_SETTING
hint: Maybe you meant ['max_threads']
context appended: 0

=== values that are fine still work
1
1
